enter","title":"Learn the Library Before You Need It","subtitle":"Saturday morning · Locate study rooms and student support","notes":"Walk both floors, identify the printers and Writing Center, then note how study-room reservations work before your first assignments arrive.","short_summary":"A short library orientation now makes later study sessions easier to plan.","evidence_claim":"JBU identifies the library in the Learning Resource Center and documents study rooms, computers, printers, the Writing Center, and IT Help Desk.","source_url":"https://www.jbu.edu/hubfs/JBU-Library-Information-Sheet.pdf?hsLang=en","source_title":"JBU Library Information Sheet","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"JBU currently lists Saturday library hours as 10 a.m.–6 p.m. and Sunday hours as 2 p.m.–2 a.m. on its commuter-resources page; academic-break hours may differ.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jbu-dogwood-trail","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Dogwood Trail","title":"Trace Dogwood Trail","subtitle":"Saturday midday · Learn the north side of campus","notes":"Follow the named trail only in daylight, keep to established walkways, and use the route to recognize the athletics and residence-side landmarks.","short_summary":"Turn a daylight walk into a low-pressure campus geography lesson.","evidence_claim":"The official JBU campus map labels Dogwood Trail on the north side of campus near Sager Creek and multiple athletics facilities.","source_url":"https://www.jbu.edu/hubfs/20240119_JBU_Map_Letter.pdf?hsLang=en","source_title":"John Brown University Campus Map","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use the official campus map and remain on marked routes. The source does not publish separate trail hours or guarantee conditions.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jbu-walton-lifetime-health-complex","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Walton Lifetime Health Complex","title":"Try a Recreation Session at Walton","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · Bring your current JBU ID","notes":"Choose one facility activity that matches your experience, bring your student ID, and review posted rules before entering a court, track, or pool area.","short_summary":"Use a first workout to learn the campus recreation facility and its entry routine.","evidence_claim":"JBU describes Walton Lifetime Health Complex as its campus fitness facility, and current facility policy accepts a current student JBU ID for admission.","source_url":"https://www.jbu.edu/hubfs/health-complex/health-complex-files/Member%20Policies%20_%20Procedures.pdf","source_title":"Walton Lifetime Health Complex Policies and Procedures","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-02-05","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Current JBU students must present their JBU ID. Facility schedules vary, so check the linked facility-hours information before visiting.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"siloam-springs-museum","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Siloam Springs Museum","title":"Put Siloam Springs in Context","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · 112 North Maxwell Street","notes":"Browse the permanent and rotating exhibits, then connect one display about the springs, local industry, or earlier residents to the town outside.","short_summary":"Add local history to the weekend without requiring an admission purchase.","evidence_claim":"The museum states that it presents permanent and rotating exhibits about Siloam Springs history and that admission is always free.","source_url":"https://www.siloamspringsmuseum.com/fc2a25e8-e254-47fb-98a1-22db4d83cccf","source_title":"Our Museum — Siloam Springs Museum","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Open Tuesday–Saturday, 10 a.m.–5 p.m., according to the museum. Admission is free; optional donations are accepted.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"bob-henry-park","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Bob Henry Park","title":"Take a Park Break at Bob Henry","subtitle":"Saturday late afternoon · 500 West Benton Street","notes":"Walk through the public park, choose a court or open recreation area that is available, and leave reserved pavilions to scheduled groups.","short_summary":"Use a named city park for an unstructured outdoor pause before returning to campus.","evidence_claim":"The City of Siloam Springs lists Bob Henry Park at 500 West Benton Street with basketball, tennis, sand volleyball, playground, skate-park, and restroom amenities.","source_url":"https://www.siloamsprings.com/Facilities/Facility/Details/Bob-Henry-Park-Pavilions-2","source_title":"Bob Henry Park Pavilions","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor amenities are city facilities; pavilion use may require a reservation. Check posted park rules, closures, and court availability on arrival.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jbu-cathedral-of-the-ozarks","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Cathedral of the Ozarks","title":"Close Sunday at The Gathering","subtitle":"Sunday evening · Student-led worship in the Cathedral","notes":"Check the current chapel calendar, arrive early enough to choose a seat, and treat attendance as a chance to observe a recurring part of JBU life.","short_summary":"End the first weekend with JBU’s documented Sunday-night, student-led worship gathering.","evidence_claim":"JBU documents The Gathering as a student-led worship experience held every Sunday night in the Cathedral of the Ozarks.","source_url":"https://www.jbu.edu/news/feature-stories/?id=184932277520","source_title":"The Gathering","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-01-15","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The source identifies Sunday-night recurrence but does not provide a current start time. Confirm the time and any calendar exception before attending.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jbu-big-games","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Big Games","title":"Finish Orientation with Big Games","subtitle":"Orientation weekend · Join your assigned team","notes":"Wear clothes suited to warm outdoor activity, follow event leaders, and participate at your comfort level while learning your larger orientation team.","short_summary":"Use JBU’s recurring team activity to close the weekend with the people in your orientation group.","evidence_claim":"JBU states that Big Games occurs at the beginning of fall Orientation and combines orientation groups into larger teams for activities and obstacles.","source_url":"https://www.jbu.edu/student-life/traditions-and-activities/","source_title":"Student Traditions & Activities at John Brown University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Big Games is limited to scheduled fall Orientation programming. Follow the current Orientation schedule and event staff’s safety directions.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
